  "status": "partial",
  "scope": "B10 Linux arm64 Broker resource-allocation pool across cache,Snapshot/latest,Gateway windows and final resource Bytes/UTF-8 aliases. Does not certify the entire Broker or Session memory footprint.",
  "implementation": {
    "limit": {
      "defaultBytes": 805306368,
      "configuration": "REMOTE_PAINT_RESOURCE_POOL_BYTES,64MiB..2GiB; deliberately small quotas can reject a working set otherwise supported under the default"
    },
    "ownership": "One atomic reservation per owned payload/wire/chunk/manifest allocation; Vec capacities are charged with buffer-owner overhead,Resource/Chunk/ChunkList metadata and vector capacity use conservative estimates. Bytes::from_owner and Utf8Bytes preserve the reservation through final aliases/slices. Shared chunks and descriptor-upgrade buffers share credit; upgraded manifest/Resource metadata reserve separately. Fields drop buffers before credit. This is not allocator usable-size/RSS accounting.",
    "admission": "Reserve before wire Vec allocation; prevent capacity growth outside admission. Incoming already-decoded payload capacity is admitted on conversion to owned Bytes; its preceding input/parser allocation is explicitly outside this pool. Budget denial drops all staged credits and preserves committed generations/resources.",
    "pressure": "Before a new map exceeds conservative headroom, retire disposable old history and strong-cache refs while retaining latest and actual peer owners. Up to256 receipts coalesce only known pressure-retired publish requests; no newer map is implicitly published. Unknown serials remain errors. Cache/history pressure policy can run before a failing map; Mapper transaction rollback itself remains exact.",
    "source": "RESOURCE_BUDGET_PRESSURE pauses display capture, preserves requested demand and page clock, polls resourceBudget at100ms while demanded, and forces resource resend on resume. A maximum one-per-second admitted trial prevents a conservative headroom estimate from stranding a smaller next frame. Close cancels timers and fences late polls; unknown RPC/capture failures remain failures.",
    "diagnostics": "mapperStats reports retained-cache and current resource-pool bytes separately; resourceBudget reports limit/used/peak/live allocations/denials/readiness. Resource pressure counters are separate from genuine capture errors."
  },
